Automatically Generate Input/Output Channel Interfaces
April 20, 2008

Howto:
Run the generateChannels.pl script to generate the basic input and output channel
interface that is used by a variety of applications that use the 
channel protocol, such as the IPC comms system and the data logger.

See './generateChannels.pl -h' for usage information.

Principal of Operation:
The channel.cpp, channel.h, and SConscript files are templates, the 
genChannel.awk script performs string substitutions on these files
to generate the actual source code that gets compiled.  The 
generateChannels.pl script is simply calling awk on the genChannel.awk 
file numerous times with the correct variables set that makes the
appropriate substitutions in the templated source files.

---

Automatically Generate TypeTraits interface
September 15, 2008

Howto:
Run the generateTypeTraits.pl script to generate an interface
that can be used by a variety of programs that need to load
a data type based on its trait and do something special with it.
An example is the csvable trait, where an arbitrary data type
can be loaded from its serialized form as a csvable object and
have its contents printed in csv format.

See './generateTypeTraits.pl -h' for usage information.

Principal of Operation:
Basically the same as generateChannel.pl, except it executes an awk
script called genTypeTraits.awk.


-- 

Combined autogen scripts into one scripts: generate.pl
January 23, 2012  (updated 03/13/2014 -- remove compression information)

./generate.pl has a new usage:

Code Generation:
-r = Restorable (generate Restorable)
--csvable / --textWritable (generate TypeTraits)
-a = All of the above (generate Channel, TypeTraits, Restorable)

SConscript-only Generation:
-s = Only generate a SConscript based off of the specified options (do not generate the code)
-f = Generates a SConscript by examining the directory structure of an existing interface

The -i, -p, and -d options are required for all of the above options with the exception of -f.  
The code generation options above can be used on an existing interface to append the specified
feature to the interface.  (i.e. if the specified interface already exists, just append the
specified generated code and write an approprioate SConscript).

Note: the interface's SConscript will be overwritten by this script.  If there are additional items specified
in an existing SConscript, they need to be re-added to the SConscript after using this script.

Note: The Channel portion of the interface is always generated if it does not exist.
